                    {
                        "sense_id": "ccc58fa8-c7f2-34f1-a246-fdd022aa3150",
                        "entry_id": "3f158f45-ce92-3fbf-9c51-e20b88afef59",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To negotiate new terms to replace old ones."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c3713ce-6c00-4f76-b9a8-4a799a5b4e38",
                                "sense_id": "ccc58fa8-c7f2-34f1-a246-fdd022aa3150",
                                "text": "The United States announced today that it had renegotiated an important agreement governing textile trade between developing nations and the industrialized countries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b762f4ef-363d-4b7f-9565-c36cbb8bb857",
                                "sense_id": "ccc58fa8-c7f2-34f1-a246-fdd022aa3150",
                                "text": "The Cordiant Communications Group in London, the troubled agency company, said yesterday that it would seek to sell additional assets to reduce debt as it renegotiates its loan agreements with banks for a second time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cc6a390-adc8-439f-af00-a5426e8ba4e6",
                                "sense_id": "ccc58fa8-c7f2-34f1-a246-fdd022aa3150",
                                "text": "The compulsion to expose, renegotiate, or reinvent the strengths and weaknesses of dance tradition offers little in its final outcome to attract the average dance-goer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "163f24f4-cb33-484e-ba3b-c9760f0d8f29",
                                "sense_id": "ccc58fa8-c7f2-34f1-a246-fdd022aa3150",
                                "text": "Ultimately, urbex remains a kind of cipher—occasionally, it catches media attention, and is grouped with other subcultures, like parkour, or even steampunk (Dawdy 2010), that are somehow \"remixing\" or renegotiating ways to relate to space, and how particular spaces are envisioned to exist within time."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
